usage: mdbx_BIN [-V] [-v[v[v...]]] [-q] [-1..9] [-t seconds] [-f percent] [-r percent] [-s megabytes] [-c] [-u|U] [-h|--help] db_pathname
  -V		print version and exit
  -v		more verbose, could be repeated for extra details from debug-enabled builds.
  -q		be quiet.
  -1		perform a single quick defragmentation cycle without two-stage moves.
  -2 .. -9	limits the number of defragmentation cycles.
  -t seconds	limits the duration of defragmentation in seconds.
  -f percent	defragment until free up a given percentage of unused space (default 100).
  -r percent	acceptable undefragmented residue in percent of used space (0 by default).
  -s megabytes	preferred defragmentation step/transaction size.
  -c		force cooperative mode (don't try exclusive).
  -u		warmup database before defragmenting.
  -U		warmup and try lock database pages in memory before defragmenting.
  -h|--help	print this usage message and exit.
  db_pathname	path to the database.
